# ── AGENT PIPELINE (SINGLE AGENT ARCHITECTURE) ──────────────

This project uses ONE Beyond Presence agent per session, not two.
The agent is created fresh for every PDF upload with document-specific prompts.

STEP 1 — api/process-document.js
  Input:  multipart/form-data with field "pdf" (PDF file)
  Action: formidable parses upload → pdf-parse extracts text →
          GPT-4o generates JSON with these exact keys:
          system_prompt, greeting, role_objectives,
          conversation_flow_structure, starting_script, document_summary
  Output: { success: true, prompts: { ...above keys }, document_summary }
  GPT-4o temperature: 0.3
  response_format: { type: "json_object" }
  system_prompt must be under 900 characters
  All values must be plain strings — no nested objects

STEP 2 — api/start-session.js
  Input:  multipart/form-data with fields: system_prompt, greeting, name (optional)
  Action: POST https://api.bey.dev/v1/agents with:
          { avatar_id: BEY_AVATAR_ID, system_prompt, greeting, name }
          Headers: { x-api-key: BEYOND_PRESENCE_API_KEY }
  Build embed URL: `https://bey.chat/embed/${agentData.id}`
  DO NOT attempt any knowledge base PDF upload — it is not a public API
  Output: { success: true, agent_id, agent_embed_url, agent_name }

STEP 3 — api/end-session.js
  Input:  JSON body: { transcript_text, agent_id, scenario_type, duration_seconds }
  Action:
    1. Grade transcript_text with GPT-4o (temperature 0.2)
    2. Insert into Supabase pitch_sessions
    3. Fire-and-forget DELETE https://api.bey.dev/v1/agents/{agent_id}
  Output: { success: true, grades: { filler_word_count, pacing_score,
            clarity_score, overall_score, top_3_improvements, critical_feedback } }
  If transcript_text is empty use: "No transcript provided for this session."

# ── GPT-4o PROMPTS ───────────────────────────────────────────

PROCESS DOCUMENT PROMPT (api/process-document.js):
System: "You are an expert at reading project documents and generating
precise AI agent configuration for a defense panel simulation.
You always output valid JSON only. No markdown, no backticks, no explanation."

User: "You are generating configuration for a hyper-critical AI defense
panel judge. Read this document completely and output ONLY a valid JSON
object with exactly these 6 keys:

system_prompt: Under 900 characters. Include: exact project name and
one sentence on what it does, exactly 3 specific technical claims with
real numbers or metrics from the document, exactly 2 budget or timeline
figures from the document, exactly 2 team roles from the document.
End with: Ask one sharp question at a time. Never accept vague answers.
Challenge every metric. Demand justification for every technology choice.

greeting: One sentence. Start with Hello. Name the project. State you
are here to critically evaluate it.

role_objectives: Max 3 sentences. Skeptical evaluator role, specific
technical areas to probe, professional but unimpressed tone.

conversation_flow_structure: Exactly 5 numbered steps as a single string.
Step 1: Core technical approach. Step 2: Challenge most ambitious claim.
Step 3: Probe budget with exact figures. Step 4: Question team capability.
Step 5: Ask for single biggest risk to project success.

starting_script: 2-3 sentences. Name project. Say proposal reviewed.
Name most technically ambitious component explicitly.

document_summary: 150-200 words plain English. Include project name,
what it does, core components, budget total, team structure, 3 most
ambitious claims.

Document: [extracted PDF text]"

END SESSION GRADING PROMPT (api/end-session.js):
System: "You are a professional presentation coach grading a defense
panel session. Output valid JSON only. No markdown, no backticks."

User: "Grade this transcript. Output ONLY JSON with these keys:
filler_word_count (number — count: um uh like basically you know
sort of kind of right so yeah),
pacing_score (1-10),
clarity_score (1-10),
overall_score (0-100),
top_3_improvements (array of 3 strings referencing what was actually said),
critical_feedback (2-3 sentences, direct, specific, references transcript)

Transcript: [transcript_text]"

