# ── ERROR HANDLING ───────────────────────────────────────────

react-hot-toast for all user-facing messages.

Success: "Document parsed successfully" | "Panel initialized" | "Session saved"
Error:   "Could not analyze document. Try a smaller PDF."
         "Could not initialize panel. Check API keys."
         "Could not save session results."
         "Connection lost. Returning to lobby."

Never show raw errors or stack traces to the user.
Always console.error internally.
Wrap all /api calls in try/catch.

# ── SUPABASE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

One table only: pitch_sessions

Schema:
  id                uuid PK default gen_random_uuid()
  created_at        timestamptz default now()
  user_id           text default 'demo-user-1'
  scenario_type     text not null
  document_summary  text
  transcript_text   text
  duration_seconds  integer default 0
  filler_word_count integer default 0
  critical_feedback text
  overall_score     integer
  bey_call_id       text
  is_active         boolean default true

src/lib/supabase.js:
  import { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js'
  export const supabase = createClient(
    import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_URL,
    import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
  )

